---
/**
 * Diagrams for the three market-coupling experiments (EEME chapter 2).
 * kind="splitting": Nordic market splitting, toggle uncongested/congested.
 * kind="trilateral": summary curves vs full order books, toggle.
 * kind="volume": volume coupling and why it failed, static.
 * Shared toggle behaviour: buttons [data-ed-btn] show/hide [data-ed-state].
 */
interface Props {
  kind: 'splitting' | 'trilateral' | 'volume';
}
const { kind } = Astro.props;
---

{
  kind === 'splitting' && (
    <figure class="not-prose border-border my-6 rounded-lg border p-4 sm:p-5" data-ed>
      <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">Market splitting, step by step</p>
        <div class="border-border flex rounded-md border p-0.5 text-xs" role="group">
          <button type="button" data-ed-btn="a" class="rounded px-2.5 py-1 font-medium transition-colors">
            Step 1: cables ignored
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-ed-btn="b" class="rounded px-2.5 py-1 font-medium transition-colors">
            Step 2: cable too small
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <svg viewBox="0 0 560 220" class="w-full select-none" aria-label="Market splitting diagram">
        <rect x="30" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <rect x="330" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="130" y="64" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1">NORTH</text>
        <text x="130" y="79" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">cheap hydro, wants to export</text>
        <text x="430" y="64" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="11" letter-spacing="1">SOUTH</text>
        <text x="430" y="79" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">more demand, pricier plants</text>
        <line x1="230" y1="118" x2="330" y2="118" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="8" opacity="0.5" />
        <text x="280" y="102" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">cable: 1,000 MW</text>

        <g data-ed-state="a">
          <rect x="30" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="var(--chart-1)" opacity="0.10" />
          <rect x="330" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="var(--chart-1)" opacity="0.10" />
          <text x="130" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="26" font-weight="700">€35</text>
          <text x="430" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="26" font-weight="700">€35</text>
          <text x="130" y="160" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">system price</text>
          <text x="430" y="160" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">system price</text>
          <path d="M245 118 H310 l-8 -6 m8 6 l-8 6" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-1)" stroke-width="2.5" />
          <text x="280" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="10">600 MW: it fits</text>
        </g>

        <g data-ed-state="b" style="display:none">
          <rect x="30" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="var(--chart-2)" opacity="0.12" />
          <rect x="330" y="40" width="200" height="140" rx="10" fill="var(--chart-3)" opacity="0.12" />
          <text x="130" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="26" font-weight="700">€30</text>
          <text x="430" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="26" font-weight="700">€40</text>
          <text x="130" y="160" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">exporting area: lower price</text>
          <text x="430" y="160" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">importing area: higher price</text>
          <path d="M245 118 H310 l-8 -6 m8 6 l-8 6" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-3)" stroke-width="2.5" />
          <text x="280" y="140" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="10">1,000 MW: full</text>
          <line x1="280" y1="30" x2="280" y2="88" stroke="var(--chart-5)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 4" />
          <text x="280" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="10" font-weight="600">market splits here</text>
        </g>
      </svg>

      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 min-h-[2.5rem] text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <span data-ed-state="a">
          Step 1: clear the whole region with one order book as if cables were
          infinite. The result is a single system price. Then check: do the
          implied flows fit on the cables? If yes, done, everyone pays €35.
        </span>
        <span data-ed-state="b" style="display:none">
          If the trade doesn't fit (the north would export 1,400 MW through a
          1,000 MW cable), split the region at the congested cable. The north
          re-clears with less export (price falls to €30), the south with less
          import (price rises to €40), and the cable carries exactly its limit.
        </span>
      </p>
      <figcaption class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 border-t pt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Nord Pool could do this from day one because it was already one
        exchange with one order book. The hard question was how to get the
        same result with <em>several</em> exchanges.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === 'trilateral' && (
    <figure class="not-prose border-border my-6 rounded-lg border p-4 sm:p-5" data-ed>
      <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium">Three exchanges, one market: two ways to try</p>
        <div class="border-border flex rounded-md border p-0.5 text-xs" role="group">
          <button type="button" data-ed-btn="a" class="rounded px-2.5 py-1 font-medium transition-colors">
            Design 1: summaries
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-ed-btn="b" class="rounded px-2.5 py-1 font-medium transition-colors">
            Design 2: full order books
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <svg viewBox="0 0 560 296" class="w-full select-none" aria-label="Trilateral market coupling diagram">
        <>
          {[
            { x: 30, name: 'APX', cc: 'NL' },
            { x: 215, name: 'Belpex', cc: 'BE' },
            { x: 400, name: 'Powernext', cc: 'FR' },
          ].map(({ x, name, cc }) => (
            <g>
              <rect x={x} y="28" width="130" height="74" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <text x={x + 65} y="48" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="12" font-weight="600">
                {name} · {cc}
              </text>
              <line x1={x + 24} y1="60" x2={x + 106} y2="60" stroke="var(--chart-2)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
              <line x1={x + 24} y1="70" x2={x + 92} y2="70" stroke="var(--chart-2)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.6" />
              <line x1={x + 24} y1="80" x2={x + 98} y2="80" stroke="var(--chart-5)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" opacity="0.6" />
              <line x1={x + 24} y1="90" x2={x + 112} y2="90" stroke="var(--chart-5)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
            </g>
          ))}
        </>
        <rect x="195" y="222" width="170" height="50" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="280" y="243" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="12" font-weight="600">central algorithm</text>
        <text x="280" y="260" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">run by the exchanges in turns</text>

        <g data-ed-state="a">
          <path d="M95 102 C 95 160, 200 190, 228 222" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-3)" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M280 102 V 222" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-3)" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M465 102 C 465 160, 360 190, 332 222" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-3)" stroke-width="2" />
          <path d="M60 118 q10 -10 20 0 q10 10 20 0" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-3)" stroke-width="2" />
          <text x="112" y="126" class="fill-foreground" font-size="10">one summary curve per hour</text>
          <text x="288" y="150" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">"at price X we'd export Y MW"</text>
          <path d="M240 272 C 160 290, 80 240, 68 112 l-5 9 m5 -9 l8 6" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted-foreground)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
          <text x="120" y="286" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">sends back volumes only; each exchange prices its own market</text>
          <text x="380" y="180" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11" font-weight="600">⚠ block orders span hours:</text>
          <text x="380" y="195" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11">a per-hour summary can't</text>
          <text x="380" y="210" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11">describe them, so the fixed</text>
          <text x="380" y="225" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11">volumes can be wrong</text>
        </g>

        <g data-ed-state="b" style="display:none">
          <path d="M95 102 C 95 160, 200 190, 228 222" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-2)" stroke-width="2.5" />
          <path d="M280 102 V 222" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-2)" stroke-width="2.5" />
          <path d="M465 102 C 465 160, 360 190, 332 222" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-2)" stroke-width="2.5" />
          <text x="112" y="126" class="fill-foreground" font-size="10">the complete order book, every single bid</text>
          <path d="M240 272 C 160 290, 80 240, 68 112 l-5 9 m5 -9 l8 6" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-2)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
          <text x="120" y="286" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">returns prices AND flows, consistent for everyone</text>
          <text x="380" y="190" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11" font-weight="600">✓ one algorithm sees</text>
          <text x="380" y="205" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11">everything, including block</text>
          <text x="380" y="220" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11">orders. Live since 2006.</text>
        </g>
      </svg>

      <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 min-h-[2.5rem] text-sm leading-relaxed">
        <span data-ed-state="a">
          Design 1 tried to keep the order books private: each exchange sends
          only a summary (the net export curve), the central step fixes the
          cross-border volumes, and each exchange prices its own market with
          those volumes locked in. Piloting showed the summaries lose too much
          information; it was abandoned before going live.
        </span>
        <span data-ed-state="b" style="display:none">
          Design 2 is the honest version: share everything, clear everything
          in one calculation. This is what went live in 2006 and what all of
          Europe runs today. The compromise for the exchanges: they jointly
          control the algorithm and take turns operating it.
        </span>
      </p>
      <figcaption class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 border-t pt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        The green and red bars inside each exchange are its order book: buy
        and sell bids. The whole design question is who gets to see them.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

{
  kind === 'volume' && (
    <figure class="not-prose border-border my-6 rounded-lg border p-4 sm:p-5" data-ed>
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-medium">Volume coupling: the summary shortcut, tried once more</p>

      <svg viewBox="0 0 560 250" class="w-full select-none" aria-label="Volume coupling diagram">
        <rect x="30" y="36" width="190" height="110" rx="10" fill="var(--chart-1)" opacity="0.08" />
        <rect x="30" y="36" width="190" height="110" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <rect x="340" y="36" width="190" height="110" rx="10" fill="var(--chart-3)" opacity="0.08" />
        <rect x="340" y="36" width="190" height="110" rx="10" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="125" y="60" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="12" font-weight="600">Nord Pool · East Denmark</text>
        <text x="435" y="60" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="12" font-weight="600">EEX · Germany</text>
        <text x="125" y="100" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="24" font-weight="700">€45</text>
        <text x="435" y="100" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="24" font-weight="700">€50</text>
        <text x="125" y="122" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">prices its market on its own</text>
        <text x="435" y="122" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">prices its market on its own</text>

        <line x1="220" y1="91" x2="340" y2="91" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="8" opacity="0.5" />
        <text x="280" y="75" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">Kontek cable</text>
        <path d="M325 91 H240 l8 -6 m-8 6 l8 6" fill="none" stroke="var(--chart-5)" stroke-width="2.5" />
        <text x="280" y="112" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="11" font-weight="600">✗ wrong-way flow</text>

        <rect x="195" y="182" width="170" height="46" rx="8" fill="none" stroke="var(--border)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        <text x="280" y="201" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground" font-size="12" font-weight="600">volume-only algorithm</text>
        <text x="280" y="217" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground" font-size="10">fixes MW on the cable from summaries</text>
        <path d="M280 182 V 130 l-6 8 m6 -8 l6 8" fill="none" stroke="var(--muted-foreground)" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 3" />
      </svg>

      <figcaption class="text-muted-foreground mt-2 border-t pt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed">
        Two years after the trilateral project dropped the summary idea, EEX
        and Nord Pool revived it: a central step fixes only the volumes on the
        cable, each exchange then sets its own price. Because the volumes were
        fixed from summaries, they could disagree with the real order books,
        and hours occurred where power was scheduled towards the cheaper side,
        exactly the explicit-auction disease coupling was meant to cure. The
        project was repaired several times and then stopped.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  )
}

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ed]').forEach((root) => {
    const buttons = root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-ed-btn]');
    if (buttons.length === 0) return;

    function show(state: string) {
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-ed-state]').forEach((el) => {
        el.style.display = el.dataset.edState === state ? '' : 'none';
      });
      buttons.forEach((b) => {
        const active = b.dataset.edBtn === state;
        b.classList.toggle('bg-muted', active);
        b.classList.toggle('text-muted-foreground', !active);
      });
    }

    buttons.forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener('click', () => show(b.dataset.edBtn!)),
    );
    show('a');
  });
</script>
